    "mode": "client-error-listener",
    "kind": "configured",
    "description": "The native mode plus an 'error' listener on every pooled client, added with pool.on('connect'), on the pool db.transaction() uses and on the pool migrate() uses. pg-pool removes its own client listener while a client is checked out, and Drizzle adds none, so in native mode a terminated backend's error event ends the process before db.transaction() or migrate() can reject. The listener does nothing else: no rollback and no connection discard.",
